{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"agent_message","text":"A plain `cargo test` intentionally skips a `cdylib`-only library when no Rust test links it. To keep the differential test self-contained—and still avoid linking or calling Rust directly—I’m adding a build helper that compiles the crate’s library source as the feature-matched test `.so` and passes only its path to the integration test. The test continues to access every Rust symbol exclusively through `libloading`."}}
